cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KVRM in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "KVRM: Registry-Constrained Decision Architectures for Audited Finite Action Spaces"
authors:
  - family-names: Price
    given-names: Robert
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/robertcprice/KVRM"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-11
abstract: >-
  KVRM is a registry-constrained decision architecture for routing among
  finite audited actions in safety-adjacent, infrastructure-adjacent, and
  enterprise domains. Decision-making is restricted to a versioned action
  registry with deterministic validation and execution boundaries between
  prediction and effect. Across nine benchmarked domains (610 cases), hybrid
  KVRM holds a 0.0 false-accept rate and 1.0 unsupported-case rejection rate,
  with perfect semantic correctness in seven domains.
keywords:
  - decision-routing
  - fail-closed
  - action-registry
  - guardrails
  - auditability
